D-Eye
=====

D-Eye is an independent, clean-room implementation. It was informed by the
architecture and security patterns of the following projects, which are NOT
bundled or copied verbatim. No source file, branding, credential, or private
API from these projects is included in D-Eye.

Design inspiration and patterns studied (not vendored):

  * Agent-Reach  -- MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Agent Eyes / "Neo Reid"
                    https://github.com/Panniantong/Agent-Reach
                    (capability-router idea; URL host-allowlist pattern re-implemented
                     and hardened into deye/core/policy.py)

  * mcpmarket-plugin (MCPmarket) -- MIT License
                    https://github.com/knoxgraeme/mcpmarket-plugin
                    (Claude plugin manifest / hook shape studied; the plugin here
                     ships NO remote token and NO remote skill-sync path.)

D-Eye is fully keyless and FOSS-first: no paid API, hosted account, or
third-party service is required by the D-Eye core.

SECURITY NOTE: the supplied mcpmarket plugin archive contained a live-looking
bearer token in its .mcp.json. That value was treated as compromised, is NOT
reproduced anywhere in D-Eye, and should be revoked/rotated by its owner.
